From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:08:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: scmi: add a boost parameter that holds from policy
 creation

With boost OPPs present (Sky1: 2.0-2.6 GHz on the A720s), scmi-cpufreq
starts with boost off, and cpuinfo.max_freq excludes them when
CPUFREQ_CREATE_POLICY sets the CPU capacities. Turning boost on later
(sysfs) raises the frequencies but leaves the capacities as they were: on a
CIX CP8180 the A520s keep 381 (403 DMIPS/MHz x 1.8 GHz against 1.9 GHz)
where 279 is right with the A720s at 2.6 GHz (the ACPI CPPC kernel reports
279), so EAS places tasks on the little cores that do not fit them.

Add scmi_cpufreq.boost=1 to start with boost enabled, and mirror the global
boost state into the policy from ->init(), before cpuinfo is computed, so the
capacities are derived from the boost frequencies.

Tested on a Minisforum MS-R1 with scmi_cpufreq.boost=1: capacities
1024/984/905/866 (A720) and 278 (A520), matching the 1024/984/906/867/279
that the vendor ACPI (CPPC) kernel reports.

Signed-off-by: hotschmoe <isaac@mass-engineering.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c
index c450cf9c8..074e64549 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/scmi-cpufreq.c
@@ -290,6 +290,13 @@ static int scmi_cpufreq_init(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 	policy->driver_data = priv;
 	policy->freq_table = freq_table;
 
+	/*
+	 * Mirror the global boost state now, not at the end of
+	 * cpufreq_online(): cpuinfo.max_freq is computed before then, and
+	 * CPUFREQ_CREATE_POLICY sets the CPU capacities from it.
+	 */
+	policy->boost_enabled = cpufreq_boost_enabled();
+
 	/* SCMI allows DVFS request for any domain from any CPU */
 	policy->dvfs_possible_from_any_cpu = true;
 
@@ -380,6 +387,10 @@ static void scmi_cpufreq_register_em(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 				    em_power_scale);
 }
 
+static bool boost;
+module_param(boost, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(boost, "Start with the boost OPPs enabled, so CPU capacities are computed from the boost frequencies");
+
 static struct cpufreq_driver scmi_cpufreq_driver = {
 	.name	= "scmi",
 	.flags	= CPUFREQ_HAVE_GOVERNOR_PER_POLICY |
@@ -464,6 +475,7 @@ static int scmi_cpufreq_probe(struct scmi_device *sdev)
 	}
 #endif
 
+	scmi_cpufreq_driver.boost_enabled = boost;
 	ret = cpufreq_register_driver(&scmi_cpufreq_driver);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "%s: registering cpufreq failed, err: %d\n",
-- 
